data.content:
In .NET 10, `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets OpenAPI v3.1. Here are the breaking changes and fixes:

## Key Changes

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.OpenApiString` | `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonValue` |
| `schema.Example = new OpenApiString(...)` | `schema.Example = JsonValue.Create(...)` |
| `property.Value.Nullable = true/false` | `property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null` (or remove the flag) |
| `new OpenApiSecurityScheme { Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ..., Id = ... } }` | `new OpenApiSchemeReference("oauth2")` |
| `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` | Removed — use typed reference classes |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null; // remove nullable
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Summary of fixes

1. **`OpenApiString` → `JsonValue.Create()`** — The `IOpenApiAny` hierarchy is gone; examples are now `JsonNode`.
2. **`Nullable` property removed** — OpenAPI 3.1 uses `type: ["string", "null"]` instead of `nullable: true`. Control it via the `JsonSchemaType.Null` flag.
3. **`OpenApiReference` pattern replaced** — Use typed reference classes like `OpenApiSchemeReference(id)`, `OpenApiSchemaReference(id)`, etc. from `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References`.
